description: When to split TS modules in ASU (domain over micro-files)
alwaysApply: true
---

# File splitting

- **Components:** under `{feature}/components/<subfeature>/` (feature-grouped, not `atoms/` / `logic/`). Context in `{feature}/context/`; hooks in `{feature}/hooks/`. Layout exports end with `Layout`; orchestration UI exports end with `Logic` (`session_screen_logic.tsx`).
- **Business logic:** group by **domain/feature file** (e.g. `practice_utils.ts`, `practice_session_view_state.ts`), not one file per micro-concern (labels, editor state, editable flags).
- **Split only** when a single file becomes too large to read or when a chunk is reused across unrelated features.
- Feature-scoped helpers go in `{feature}_utils.ts`; app-wide helpers stay in `core/utils/`.